# .dockerignore for Mentora.API/Dockerfile
# Build context is the repo root (docker build -f Mentora.API/Dockerfile .).
# The Dockerfile's `COPY . .` (build stage) pulls in everything below that
# isn't excluded here, and dotnet publish auto-copies every appsettings*.json
# it finds alongside the .csproj into the final image.

# Security fix (E1.3): appsettings.Development.json carries a local DB
# password and RefreshTokenPurge.InitialDelayMinutes=0. The container runs
# ASPNETCORE_ENVIRONMENT=Development, so this file overrides appsettings.json
# and defeats the 15-minute purge delay guard. Must never reach the image.
# appsettings.json and appsettings.Production.json are NOT excluded.
**/appsettings.Development.json

# Build artifacts from the host (Mentora.API/Mentora.Core/Mentora.Infrastructure
# each have bin/ and obj/, ~49MB total today). `dotnet build`/`dotnet publish`
# regenerate these inside the container; copying host artifacts in bloats the
# context and can leak host-OS/arch-specific output.
bin
obj

# Git metadata (~5.2MB) - version history, not needed to build or run the app.
.git

# IDE/editor state - not needed to build or run the app.
.vs
.vscode

# Project documentation (~1.2MB) - not needed to build or run the app.
docs

# Stray local artifacts, e.g. `docker save` tarballs left in the repo root
# (found one at repo root today, ~95MB) - never needed as build input and
# would otherwise dominate the build context size.
*.tar

# No JS/Node tooling in this repo today, but excluding defensively in case
# any project ever adds one - node_modules is always regenerable and huge.
**/node_modules
